From 2c0b22cb5b75bd6cae7a936b211ba8c081f849e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:37:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(plugins): give plugins an authenticated way to reach
 the host API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The plugin docs contradict themselves: Security Model states a plugin cannot
reach authentication tokens or the host's localStorage, while the WebSocket
example in Plugin System Overview tells plugins to read
localStorage['auth-token']. The second one is what actually works, since the
module is imported into the same realm through a Blob URL. Any plugin needing
host data has to scrape the token today.

This adds api.host with three members. fetch() is GET-only, restricted to the
/api/ prefix, resolved same-origin with traversal rejected, and any
Authorization the plugin passes is dropped — the host attaches its own
credentials through the existing authenticatedFetch. startNewSession() and
openSession() cover the two navigation actions that have no HTTP equivalent.

api.hostApiVersion and api.surface are additive; plugins that do not know about
host keep working unchanged. Mutations and permission gating are deliberately
out of scope.
