From 6f98c53d8c494ba20941b9820ca72df062d2f7d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 01:13:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(plugins): keep the traversal check to the path, not
 the query

normalizePluginHostPath ran its '..' check over the whole raw string, so a
query value carrying two dots was refused: /api/search?q=version..next is an
ordinary search term, not traversal, and the plugin got a blocked-request
error instead of results.

The checks now run on the pathname the URL parser produces. That also resolves
'..' and its encoded spellings for us, so /api/%2e%2e/secret is rejected by
where it lands rather than by how it is spelled, and the returned path is the
normalised one. Raw whitespace stays refused in the path, where it is
malformed, and allowed in the query, where the parser encodes it.

Raised by CodeRabbit on PR #1191.
